.\" kettle.1 - manual page for kettle terminal emulator
.\" Format: man-pages macros. Render preview: `man -l packaging/linux/kettle.1`
.\" Render to text: `groff -man -Tutf8 packaging/linux/kettle.1 | less`
.TH KETTLE 1 "2026-07-14" "kettle" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
kettle \- fast, cross-platform, GPU-accelerated terminal emulator
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kettle
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ \-e
.IR PROGRAM " [" ARGS... ]]
.br
.B kettle exec
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.B \-\-
.IR CMD ...
.br
.B kettle ctl
.I METHOD
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B kettle mcp
.RI [ \-\-self\-test ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kettle
is a Rust-based terminal emulator combining the best ideas of
.BR Ghostty ,
.BR Terminator ,
.BR kitty ,
.B Alacritty
and
.B WezTerm
into one tool. Cross-platform (Linux, macOS, Windows), GPU-accelerated
via
.BR wgpu ,
and built on the battle-tested
.B alacritty_terminal
VT engine.
.PP
Features include split panes (Terminator-style binary tree),
multiple tabs with drag-to-reorder, live tear-off into a new
window (running programs move untouched), + activity / silence /
bell indicators, inline images (sixel, kitty graphics, iTerm2
inline image protocols), OSC 8 hyperlinks, OSC 133
shell-integration jump-to-prompt, ligatures, infinite scrollback,
fuzzy-search overlays (command palette, themes, SSH-host
launcher), undo close tab, duplicate tab/pane, per-window accent
colors, and broadcast / group-input mode.
.PP
Without arguments
.B kettle
launches a windowed session running the user's default shell.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Launch
.TP
.BI \-e \ "PROGRAM \fR[\fIARGS...\fR]"
Run
.I PROGRAM
instead of the default shell. Everything after
.B \-e
is treated as the command and its arguments.
.TP
.BI \-\-working-directory \ "DIR" \fR,\fP\fB\ \-d\ \fIDIR
Set the initial working directory for the launched program.
Hard-fails with a non-zero exit status if
.I DIR
does not exist (catches typos at launch time, not at the first
.B cd
inside the running shell).
.TP
.B \-\-new\-process
Force an isolated Kettle process for a default launch. With no arguments, a
launcher click normally asks the primary Kettle process to open another OS
window; every launch carrying other arguments is already isolated.
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ FILE
Load configuration from
.I FILE
instead of the auto-detected path. Hard-fails if the path doesn't exist.
.
.SS Introspection (prints and exits)
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version string (with the git SHA on git checkouts) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print every flag and its description.
.TP
.B \-\-config-path
Print the resolved config-file path (or the fallback message if no
config is loaded) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Validate the resolved config and print every effective setting +
diagnostic lines for unknown keys / malformed values.
.TP
.B \-\-print-default-config
Print every option with its default value, in the Ghostty-style
.RI """ key " = " value """
format. Useful as a starting point for
.IR ~/.config/kettle/config .
.TP
.B \-\-gpu-info
Print the
.B wgpu
adapter / backend / driver / texture-limit details kettle would
use on this machine. Useful for "blank window" / "no GPU adapter"
bug reports.
.TP
.B \-\-list-themes
Print every bundled theme name (>500 themes, sourced from the
Ghostty + iTerm2-Color-Schemes sets).
.TP
.B \-\-list-actions
Print every recognized keybind action name + every alias.
.TP
.B \-\-list-keybinds
Print every active keybind (default + user-overridden), grouped
by trigger.
.TP
.B \-\-list-ssh-hosts
Print every
.BR ssh-host
declaration in the config + every freeform host kettle has cached
from prior
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
launcher use.
.TP
.B \-\-list-layouts
Print every saved layout name
.RI ( "<config-dir>/layouts/*.json" ).
Launch one with
.BR "\-\-layout NAME" .
.TP
.B \-\-list-profiles
Print every named config profile
.RI ( "<config-dir>/profiles/*.config" ).
Launch one with
.BR "\-\-profile NAME" .
.TP
.B \-m ", " \-\-maximise ", " \-\-maximize
Maximise the window at launch (Terminator parity). Overrides the
.B window-state
config for this launch.
.TP
.B \-f ", " \-\-fullscreen
Fullscreen the window at launch. Overrides
.B window-state
for this launch.
.TP
.B \-b ", " \-\-borderless
Launch with no window decorations. Overrides the
.B borderless
config for this launch.
.TP
.B \-H ", " \-\-hidden
Launch hidden \(em useful for a Quake-style dropdown paired with a
global hotkey bound to
.BR "kettle \-\-toggle" .
When combined with
.B \-m
or
.BR \-f ,
hidden wins (then fullscreen, then maximise).
.TP
.BI \-T \ "TEXT" ", " \-\-title \ "TEXT"
Force the window title to
.I TEXT
for this launch, overriding
.BR window-title-format .
.TP
.BI \-\-shell-integration \ "SHELL"
Print the OSC 133 shell-integration snippet for
.I SHELL
(one of:
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " powershell ).
Append to your rc file to enable jump-to-prompt
.RB ( "Ctrl+Up" " / " "Ctrl+Down" )
inside kettle:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --shell-integration bash >> ~/.bashrc
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-print-completions \ SHELL
Print a tab-completion script for the kettle CLI in
.IR SHELL 's
native format. Supports
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " powershell ", "
and
.BR elvish .
.
.SS Debug / capture
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot \ PATH
Render one frame of the canonical kettle layout (single pane,
using the configured or default theme) to a PNG file at
.IR PATH .
Honors
.BR \-\-cols ", " \-\-rows ", and " \-\-config .
Used by the visual-regression CI smoke + the
.IR docs/PERFORMANCE.md
baseline.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot-menu \ PATH
Same as
.B \-\-screenshot
but renders with a synthetic right-click context menu open over
the pane. Useful for visually verifying the menu's render path
without an interactive window, and for pixel-level visual-
regression tests in CI.
.TP
.BI \-\-cols \ "N\fR, \fP\fB\-\-rows \ N"
Override the rendered grid size (in cells) for
.BR \-\-screenshot " / " \-\-screenshot-menu .
Default 96x28.
.TP
.BI \-\-tab\-handoff \ PATH
.B Deprecated
(receive parsing kept for one release, for handoff files written
by older kettles). Restore a tab from a JSON handoff file.
Nothing writes these files any more: tab tear-off is now a live
in-process move \(em drag a tab outside the window, or use the
.B move_tab_to_new_window
action \(em and the tab's running programs, PTYs and scrollback
transfer to the new window untouched.
The handoff file is deleted after read (one-shot).
.TP
.BI \-\-tab\-handoff\-fd \ FD
.B Deprecated
receive-side counterpart of
.BR \-\-tab\-handoff :
accept a tab handoff via SCM_RIGHTS over the named inherited
file descriptor. kettle no longer sends these (see above).
Unix-only.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-send \ TEXT
Send
.I TEXT
to the running kettle's focused pane via the file-based IPC.
Cross-platform (no D-Bus needed). Pair with
.B \-\-remote\-file
to address a non-default kettle instance.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-file \ PATH
Override the IPC drop path used by
.B \-\-remote\-send " / " \-\-toggle .
Default is the per-user state dir; useful when running multiple
kettle instances each with their own remote-control endpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show / hide the running kettle window (Yakuake / Tilda / Ghostty
quick-terminal parity). Bind a compositor / DE / OS
global hotkey to
.B kettle \-\-toggle
for one-key drop-down access.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile \ NAME
Launch with the named profile. Profiles live in the
config file as
.B profile = name=...
entries — argv-supplied profile overrides the default-startup one
without editing the config.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout \ NAME
Restore a named saved layout on startup. Layouts are stored
under
.IR ~/.config/kettle/layouts/ " ;"
see
.B Action::SaveLayoutAs " / " Action::RestoreLayout
for in-window save/restore.
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Restore the previous session (windows, tabs, splits, working
directories) for this launch \(em every saved window reopens at its
(monitor-clamped) saved position. By default kettle opens a fresh window \(em a single
pane in the default working directory, matching mainstream terminals.
Use this flag for a one-shot "continue where I left off" without setting
.B restore-session = true
in the config.
.TP
.BI \-\-agent\-server \ MODE
Enable kettle's agent control server for this launch, overriding the
.B agent\-server
config key.
.B MODE
is one of
.BR off ", " read\-only ", or " full .
The server is a local\-IPC surface (Unix socket / Windows named pipe) that
.BR "kettle ctl" ", " "kettle mcp" ", or an AI agent can drive: list panes,"
read the screen, and (in
.BR full )
send text + run commands. OFF by default. See
.B docs/AGENT.md
for the threat model.
.TP
.BI \-\-accent \ COLOR
Pin this window's chrome tint (peacock parity) to the
named or hex color. Accepts
.B "#RRGGBB"
or any palette name from
.BR \-\-list\-themes .
Per-window accents are on by default
.RB ( "accent\-color = auto" ):
every window \(em deduped across all kettle windows and processes
\(em claims a distinct theme-pool hue, so multiple windows are
visually distinct without any flag. Set the
.B accent\-color
config key to
.BR theme ", " off ", or " none
to opt out; a hex value (or this flag) pins one color.
.TP
.BI \-\-lua\-script \ PATH
Load
.I PATH
as the init script instead of the default
.IR ~/.config/kettle/init.lua .
The script runs in the
.B lua-sandbox = safe
sandbox by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-annotate \ TEXT
Overlay
.I TEXT
as a single caption along the bottom of the
.B \-\-screenshot
/
.B \-\-screenshot\-menu
output (iTerm2 "annotated screenshot" parity). A single non-repeatable bottom
caption \(em not a per-cell annotation.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-default\-config
Write the embedded default configuration to the resolved config path, creating
the parent directory, then exit. Refuses to overwrite an existing file. The
easiest cross-platform way to bootstrap a config \(em preferred over a shell
redirect on Windows PowerShell, whose
.B >
writes UTF-16.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-update
Check the authenticated stable release feed once for a newer kettle version,
print the result, and exit. This explicit command bypasses the background
throttle and update policy.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Interactive convenience alias for
.BR "kettle update" .
.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
The bare
.B kettle
command (above) is the GUI launcher. These subcommands are the
non-interactive / agent control surface; each returns before any window or GPU
work. See
.B docs/AGENT.md
for the full reference and threat model.
.TP
.B kettle exec \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-\- \fICMD\fR...
Run
.I CMD
under a real PTY, headlessly, and stream its output to stdout (the
non-interactive counterpart to the GUI). Propagates the child's exit code;
.B 124
on
.BR \-\-timeout ,
.B 125
on an internal error. Options:
.B \-\-cols
.IR N " / " \fB\-\-rows\fP " " N
(terminal size; default: probe the console, else 80x24),
.B \-\-cwd
.IR DIR " (also " \fB\-d\fP " " DIR ;
working directory, default inherit),
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
(kill + exit 124 after
.IR SECS ),
.B \-\-strip\-ansi
(emit plain text — good for assertions),
.B \-\-json
(one JSON object per line: start / output / title / exit), and
.BI \-\-record " PATH"
(also save an asciicast trace). The trace must be secured before the child is
started; a recording error exits with status 125 instead of running unaudited.
Capture is output-only and stops on a complete asciicast event boundary before
512 MiB; a later write failure stops the trace without killing the child.
Piped or redirected stdin is forwarded to the child on Unix and WSL. An
interactive terminal stdin is left attached to the caller, and native Windows
ConPTY stdin forwarding remains disabled.
.TP
.B kettle ctl \fIMETHOD\fR \fR[\fB\-\-pane \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-json \fIJSON\fR] [\fB\-\-text \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-pid \fIPID\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\fR]
Drive a running kettle's agent control server.
.I METHOD
is one of
.BR get_state ", " list_tabs ", " list_panes ", " read_screen ", " read_cells ", " ui_geometry ", " screenshot ", " send_text ", " send_keys ", " dispatch_keybind ", " send_mouse ", " resize_window ", " perform_action ", " wait_for ", " run_command ,
or
.B events
to stream the event feed. The target kettle must run with
.B agent\-server
enabled (see
.BR \-\-agent\-server ).
.B \-\-pane
targets a specific pane (else the focused pane);
.B \-\-json
passes method parameters as a JSON object;
.B \-\-text
is the text for
.B send_text
or the command line for
.BR run_command ;
.B \-\-pid
selects a specific kettle (else the newest running server); and
.B \-\-raw
prints the raw JSON result instead of a pretty summary.
Large list, screen, and cell reads return
.BR snapshot ,
.BR next_cursor ,
and
.BR truncated ;
continue with JSON
.BR cursor / snapshot
parameters. Requests are capped at 1 MiB and responses at 768 KiB.
.TP
.B kettle mcp \fR[\fB\-\-self\-test\fR]
Run a Model Context Protocol server over stdio, exposing kettle as native agent
tools (run a command, drive a running kettle). Supports MCP 2025-11-25 and
2025-06-18 with bounded concurrent tool execution and cancellation. Register
with Claude Code:
.B claude mcp add kettle \-\- kettle mcp\fR.
.B \-\-self\-test
runs an in-process handshake +
.B tools/list
+ one
.B kettle_run
and exits, for CI.
.TP
.B kettle update \fR[\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Download and install the latest authenticated stable release. Supported for
official installer-owned Windows x86_64 and Linux x86_64/aarch64 layouts; other
installs are refused with package-manager guidance. Verifies an Ed25519-signed
manifest, exact archive size, and SHA-256 before transactional replacement.
Running windows are not restarted. Windows stages verified files for an
out-of-process helper that waits for every Kettle process to exit; invalid or
three-times-failed pending state is quarantined on a best-effort basis so the
intact old build can start even when evidence cannot be moved. Source and
dev-record ownership markers are refused. Without
.BR \-\-yes ,
an interactive confirmation is required.
.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Defaults (every binding remappable via
.IR ~/.config/kettle/config 's
.B keybind
entries). Cmd is the macOS modifier; Ctrl on Linux / Windows.
.SS Tabs
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+T
new tab
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+1 ... Ctrl+Shift+9
new tab running the Nth entry of the new-tab dropdown (action
.BR new_tab_shell_N ,
1-based; also spelled
.BR new\-tab\-shell\-N )
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+W
close focused pane (or tab if last pane)
.TP
.B Ctrl+PgUp
previous tab
.TP
.B Ctrl+PgDn
next tab
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+PgUp
move tab left
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+PgDn
move tab right
.TP
.B Alt+1 ... Alt+9
jump to tab N by number
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+I
new window
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Q
close window
.TP
.B F11
toggle fullscreen
.PP
The new-tab button's dropdown lists every detected shell in Windows
Terminal order \(em PowerShell, Windows PowerShell, Command Prompt,
WSL distros, Visual Studio 2022 Developer Command Prompt /
PowerShell (vswhere-detected), Git Bash \(em plus Settings, Command
palette and About rows; it is always visible on every platform.
Menu rows show right-aligned shortcut hints taken from the live
keybind map.
.PP
Dragging a tab past the tab bar tears it off instantly into a live
window in the same process that rides the pointer in the OS's native
move loop \(em the tab's running programs, PTYs and scrollback move
untouched, and the window inherits the source window's size. Dropping
a torn window onto another kettle window's tab bar merges the tab
there at the marked insertion slot (the dragged window turns
translucent over the target strip on Windows); dragging a lone-tab
window's tab drags the whole window, which is how a torn-off window
re-docks. Esc before the tear cancels. On Wayland, where clients
cannot position windows, the tear happens at release instead. The
.B move_tab_to_new_window
action (alias
.BR detach_tab )
performs the same live move from the keyboard.
.SS Splits / panes
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+O
split top/bottom (Terminator-exact)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+E
split left/right (Terminator-exact)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A
auto-split (longest axis)
.TP
.B Alt+arrow
focus pane up / down / left / right
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
focus next pane (DFS order)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
focus previous pane
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+X
toggle pane zoom (maximize / restore)
.PP
Additional actions available via the command palette
.RB ( Ctrl+Shift+K ):
.BR UndoCloseTab ,
.BR DuplicateTab ,
.BR DuplicatePane ,
.BR Reset ,
and
.B about
(open the About panel \(em version, update status, GitHub link;
aliases
.BR show_about " / " show\-about )
\(em not default-bound (bind via the
.B keybind
config entry if you want a hotkey).
.SS Overlays
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+K
command palette (fuzzy actions)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
find in scrollback (regex + smart-case)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+H
URL / path quick-select hints
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
SSH-host launcher
.SS Scrollback / clipboard
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
copy selection
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V
paste (bracketed if app enabled it)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Up
jump to previous OSC 133 prompt
.TP
.B Ctrl+Down
jump to next OSC 133 prompt
.SS Scrollback movement
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down
scroll one line
.TP
.B PageUp/PageDown
scroll one page
.SS Vi-mode (Alacritty parity)
Enter vi-mode for the focused pane's scrollback. A magenta hollow
block marks the vi cursor; the terminal cursor stays in place so
you can see both. Movement, visual selection, and yank all live
on standard vi keys.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Space
toggle vi-mode (enter / exit)
.TP
.B h j k l
move vi cursor left / down / up / right
.TP
.B arrow keys
same as h/j/k/l
.TP
.B 0 ^
jump to line start
.TP
.B $
jump to line end
.TP
.B g H
jump to top of viewport
.TP
.B G L
jump to bottom of viewport
.TP
.B M
jump to middle of viewport
.TP
.B v
toggle char-visual selection (anchor at cursor)
.TP
.B y
yank visual selection to clipboard, exit vi-mode
.TP
.B Esc
exit vi-mode
.SS Quake / dropdown mode
.TP
.B kettle \-\-toggle
flip the running window's visibility, sent via the remote-control
IPC. Bind your compositor / DE / OS global hotkey to this for
Quake / Yakuake / Tilda dropdown UX.
.SS Group / broadcast
.TP
.B Super+G
toggle broadcast (group-input) on this tab
.TP
.B Shift+Super+G
turn broadcast off
.SS Font size
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Plus
increase font size
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Minus
decrease font size
.TP
.B Ctrl+0
reset font size to the configured default
.SS Pane resize
.TP
.B Shift+Arrow
resize the focused split (up / down / left / right). Composes
with split-tree weights so adjacent panes grow proportionally.
.SS Scroll
.TP
.B Shift+PgUp
.TQ
.B Shift+PgDn
scroll one page up / down through scrollback
.TP
.B Shift+Home
.TQ
.B Shift+End
jump to scrollback top / bottom
.SS Right-click
A right click anywhere in a pane opens a context menu with:
Copy / Paste / Split Right / Split Down / Close Pane / New Tab.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration lives at
.IR ~/.config/kettle/config
(Linux and macOS \(em the resolver is
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
\(->
.IR $HOME/.config ,
so macOS uses the same
.I ~/.config
path, not
.IR ~/Library ),
or
.IR %APPDATA%\\kettle\\config
(Windows). Format is Ghostty-style
.RI """ key " = " value """
lines; everything after
.B #
is a comment.
.PP
See
.B kettle\ \-\-print\-default\-config
for every option with its default + inline docstring, and the
.B kettle
docs at
.UR https://github.com/Reddimus/kettle/blob/main/docs/CONFIG.md
.UE
for the full reference.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Program kettle launches when no
.B \-e
is given.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard
.B tracing-subscriber EnvFilter
filter (e.g.
.IR info ", " debug ", " "kettle=trace" ).
Default
.I warn
surfaces session-restore failures, GPU init errors, and winit/Wayland protocol
failures on stderr.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Linux/Unix config root (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B KETTLE_VERSION " / " KETTLE_PREFIX
Used by
.B scripts/install-online.sh
(the curl-pipe installer), not the
.B kettle
binary itself.
.B KETTLE_VERSION
pins which release to download;
.B KETTLE_PREFIX
overrides the install root.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kettle/config
User config file (Linux). See CONFIGURATION above.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kettle/sessions/
Session JSON (atomic write-then-rename) capturing every window:
tabs, splits, working directories + window geometry. Always saved on exit
in restore mode; replayed on the next launch only when restore is opted
in via
.B restore-session = true
or the
.B \-\-restore
flag (off by default \(em a new window opens fresh). Failures are logged
via
.BR log::warn! .
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/kettle
Default install location for the
.B scripts/install.sh
+
.B install-online.sh
paths.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/kettle.desktop
XDG launcher (GNOME Activities / KDE Krunner / rofi).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/kettle.svg
Scalable launcher icon (plus PNG fallbacks at 16 / 24 / 32 / 48 / 64 / 128 / 256).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Launch a windowed kettle running
.BR htop :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle -e htop
.EE
.RE
.PP
Validate the resolved config and exit:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --check-config
.EE
.RE
.PP
Generate a fresh config file with every option commented:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --print-default-config > ~/.config/kettle/config
.EE
.RE
.PP
Diagnose a rendering bug (capture for issue report):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kettle --gpu-info > /tmp/gpu.txt
kettle --screenshot /tmp/kettle.png
.EE
.RE
.
